  "final_output": "## Root cause\nAt 08:20 UTC, infra moved the cart Redis to a smaller instance (config change \"Move cart Redis to a smaller instance to cut cost\", FIN-212). Each cart pod lost its connection to `cart-redis-2g` and then logged \"redis connected\" to `cart-redis-1g` with `maxmemory_mb=640` and `maxmemory_policy=noeviction`. With noeviction, Redis does not remove old keys. Cart data grows with traffic. Redis memory went from about 595 MB at 08:24 to about 640 MB at 11:10 UTC, and it stays flat at the limit from then. Since 11:10, Redis rejects writes with \"OOM command not allowed when used memory > 'maxmemory'\". So `POST /cart/items` fails with HTTP 500.\n\n## Evidence\n- Alert: `ServiceErrorRateHigh` for cart (25.2%) and gateway (4.6%) at 11:15 UTC. `RedisMemoryHigh` is not firing, so it gave no warning.\n- `get_service_health` cart, 11:00-12:00: error rate is 0 until 11:10, then up to 39.8% (38.9% at 12:00). Latency and CPU are normal.\n- `top_endpoints` cart: `POST /cart/items` fails in 85 of 89 sampled requests. `GET /cart` and `DELETE /cart/items/:id` have no errors.\n- `log_patterns` cart: new error \"add to cart failed\" (85 logs, first at 11:10:02). Trace f3e5c8692483e156ff7393b805e5e805 shows the Redis HSET step fails with the OOM error.\n- `db_health` redis and `redis_memory_used_mb`: flat at 637-640 MB from 11:10 to 12:00. Redis is up and its latency is normal (about 1 ms). So Redis is full, not slow.\n- `list_changes`: cart config change at 08:20 (move to a smaller instance) and cart deploy v2.1.0 at 09:40 (\"Upgrade Redis client library\").\n- `search_logs` cart \"redis\", 08:20: pod logs show `maxmemory_mb=640`, `noeviction`, and the new host `cart-redis-1g`.\n- The v2.1.0 deploy is not the cause. The cart error rate stays near 0 (avg 0.05%, max 0.3%) from 09:40 to 11:00, and the error comes from the Redis server, not from the client library.\n\n## Customer impact\nSince 11:10 UTC, customers cannot add items to their cart. About 19,000 add-to-cart requests failed up to 12:00 (cart_errors_per_min is about 380 per minute from 11:20, 382 at 12:00; the average over 11:00 to 12:00 is about 320). Customers can still see their cart and remove items. Fewer customers start a checkout: checkout attempts fell from about 28 per minute (10:30 to 11:10) to about 19 per minute (11:10 to 12:00), which is -33% or about 470 fewer in 50 minutes. Checkout success rate stays normal (about 97%) for the customers who have a cart. The problem is still active at 12:00 UTC.\n\n## Next steps\n1. Raise Redis `maxmemory` for the cart back to the old size (about 2 GB, host `cart-redis-2g`), or move the cart Redis back to the larger instance. Do this now.\n2. Check that cart error rate and `cart_errors_per_min` return to 0, and that add to cart works.\n3. Do not roll back cart v2.1.0. It is not related.\n4. Later: set a TTL or an eviction policy for cart keys, and make `RedisMemoryHigh` use the real `maxmemory` of the instance."
